  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Rule of Law Responses to Conflict-Related Sexual Violence in Syria</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to strengthen national capacities in Syria to prevent and respond to conflict-related sexual violence (CRSV) through the establishment of a coordinated, survivor-centred, and rule-of-law-based approach. It focuses on developing a shared competency framework across medical, legal, and psychosocial sectors, while creating a roster of qualified national experts who can be mobilized to support transitional justice and institutional processes. By enhancing coordination among key national institutions and promoting standardized professional practices, the project contributes to more effective, holistic, and rights-based responses to CRSV. It also supports national ownership by equipping institutions with the tools, expertise, and mechanisms needed to address both past and ongoing cases, ensuring accountability and improved service delivery for survivors</narrative>
  </description>
